    "reason": "The English lemma 'boss' (concept-core-boss, general, daily_life) implies a general superior or person in charge. While 'boss' is listed as one of the glosses for 監督, 監督 primarily refers to a director, supervisor, or coach, implying a specific role of overseeing a project or team (e.g., film director, sports coach, construction foreman). It is not the most general or natural term for 'boss' in everyday contexts for a general learner. The Japanese expression is semantically narrower than the general English concept.",
